## Acceptance

In order to get any license under these terms, you must agree to them as
both strict obligations and conditions on all licenses granted to you under
these terms.

Once you agree, the license grant below immediately begins, for as long as
you continue to meet the conditions below.  Failure to meet the conditions,
or the notice requirements in the Notices section, terminates the license.

## Copyright License

The licensor grants you a copyright license for the software to do
everything you might do that would otherwise infringe the licensor's
copyright in it, for any permitted purpose.  However, you may only
distribute the software according to [Distribution License](#distribution-license) and make changes or new works based on the software according to [Changes and New Works License](#changes-and-new-works-license).

## Distribution License

The licensor grants you an additional copyright license to distribute
copies of the software.  Your license to distribute covers distributing the
software with changes and new works permitted by [Changes and New Works License](#changes-and-new-works-license).

## Notices

You must ensure that anyone who gets a copy of any part of the software
from you also gets a copy of these terms.

If you make changes or new works based on the software, you must ensure
that anyone who gets a copy of any part of the software or changes or new
works based on the software from you also gets a copy of these terms, and
you must ensure that anyone who gets a copy of the software or changes or
new works based on the software from you also gets a copy of the source
code of the software, changes, or new works, as the case may be.

If you make changes or new works based on the software, you must include
prominent notices stating that you have made changes or new works based on
the software, and the date of each change or new work, in a reasonably
calculate-able location in or adjacent to the changes or new works.

## Changes and New Works License

The licensor grants you an additional copyright license to make changes
and new works based on the software for any permitted purpose.

## Patent License

The licensor grants you a patent license for the software that covers
patent claims the licensor can license, or becomes able to license, that
you would infringe by making the software or by making changes or new works
based on the software, for any permitted purpose.  However, this patent
license does not cover patent claims the licensor can license, or becomes
able to license, that you would infringe by distributing the software, or
by making, using, selling, offering for sale, having made, importing,
licensing, or exporting changes or new works based on the software,
despite the patent license above covering those patent claims for the
software itself.

## Noncommercial Purposes

Any noncommercial purpose is a permitted purpose.  Any purpose is a
noncommercial purpose where:

1.  it is not primarily intended for or directed towards commercial
    advantage or private monetary compensation, and
2.  neither the purpose itself, nor the software use underlying the
    purpose, replaces the software used for substantially the same
    purpose by parties who would otherwise need to pay a license fee to
    the licensor for the software or pay for the software.

For the purposes of this section, "commercial advantage or private
monetary compensation" includes, but is not limited to:

1.  selling the software or changes or new works based on the software,
2.  using the software, changes, or new works to provide services for a
    fee, or
3.  bundling or integrating the software, changes, or new works into a
    product or service offered for a fee.

## Personal Uses

Personal use for research, experiment, and testing for the benefit of
public knowledge and personal study, private study, learning, and
scholarship is a noncommercial purpose.  Personal uses for another purpose
are noncommercial only if they meet both conditions of [Noncommercial
Purposes](#noncommercial-purposes) above.

## Noncommercial Organizations

Use by a charitable organization, educational institution, or public
research organization, that does not operate for a fee for its services,
is a permitted purpose.  Operating for a fee includes charging for
services, receiving payment for the software, or receiving payment
related to use of the software.

Educational institutions may charge tuition, and public research
organizations may receive grants and other funding, without losing their
status as such.  However, an educational institution, charitable
organization, or public research organization operating for a fee in some
other manner, such as operating a business for profit, is not a
noncommercial organization for purposes of these terms.

## Fair Use

You may have "fair use" rights for the software under the law.  These
terms do not limit them.

## No Other Rights

These terms do not allow you to sublicense or transfer any of your
licenses to anyone else, or distribute the software under any different
terms.  You must comply strictly with these terms.  If you use the
software for any purpose beyond the scope of these terms, or in a way
that conflicts with any of the conditions of these terms, your license
terminates immediately and the licensor reserves all rights and
remedies.

If you make changes or new works based on the software, and distribute
them in violation of these terms, the licensor may recall all copies of
the software, changes, or new works that you have distributed.

## Patent Defense

If you make a written claim that the software, changes or new works based
on the software, or any product or service you offer using the software,
changes, or new works, infringes or contributes to infringement of any
patent, your patent license for the software granted under these terms
ends immediately.  If your patent license ends for this reason, your
copyright license also ends immediately.

## Violations

The first time you are notified in writing that you have violated any of
these terms, or done anything with the software not covered by your
licenses, your licenses continue nonetheless.

Your licenses end permanently if you do any of the following within 30
days of that notice:

1.  correct all violations,
2.  pay all damages due under your licenses, and
3.  notify the licensor in writing that you have corrected all violations
    and paid all damages.

Your licenses end automatically and permanently if you are notified in
writing of a violation a second time, for the same or a different
violation, or if you are notified of a violation and do not correct it
within 30 days.

If your licenses end under the previous paragraph, all sublicenses that
you have granted under your licenses end when and as your licenses end.
Your licenses end without notice if you violate these terms in a way that
notifies all recipients of the software under your licenses of your
violation.

## No Liability

**As far as the law allows, the software comes as is, without any
warranty or condition, and the licensor will not be liable to you for any
damages arising out of these terms or the use or nature of the software,
under any kind of legal claim, however it arises.  The licensor will
never be liable to you for any special, indirect, consequential, or
loss of profits damages, however they arise, even if the licensor knew
they were possible.**

## Definitions

**The licensor** is the individual or entity offering these terms, and
**the software** is the software the licensor offers under these terms.

**"You"** refers to the individual or entity agreeing to these terms.

**"Your company"** is any legal entity, sole proprietorship, or other
kind of organization that you work for, plus all organizations that have
control over, are under the control of, or are under common control with
that organization.  **Control** means ownership of substantially all the
assets of an entity, or the power to direct its management and policies,
such as ownership, management, or contractual rights of a majority of the
assets or voting shares of an entity.

**Use** means anything you do with the software requiring one of your
licenses.

